{
  "what": "Quantitative read-back evidence that the fp32 PTQ arm `fp32-s3-r14n8-wm-w5a8` realizes the SAME attention weight grid as the W8A8 QAT article `runs/9cc6e336/w8a8-s3-r14n8`, so that a synthesis of the two isolates GRID PROVENANCE (QAT vs PTQ) at EQUAL realized weight width.",
  "date": "2026-09-03",
  "method": "emitted firmware only: firmware/weights/w*.txt (the values compiled into the netlist) and firmware/defines.h. No driver flag, no Keras object. Tool: bnjettag/code/hgq2/weight_grid_audit.py.",
  "correction_to_memo_C1_3": "CORRECTION C1.3 states W8A8's realized attention weight grid is '6-bit / 5 fractional bits'. Measured here from the emitted arrays: the FRACTIONAL width is confirmed at 5 (LSB 2^-5 = 0.03125), but the realized TOTAL width is 5, not 6: pooled absmax 0.4375 fits ap_fixed<5,0> (i = -1). The '6-bit' figure is the named typedef ap_fixed<6,1> that hls4ml emits for the DENSE layers, which is a different set of arrays. The fractional width is the load-bearing quantity (it fixes the lattice and hence strength-reducibility), and it is confirmed.",
  "why_W5_and_not_W6": "convert_fp32.py's intW_absmax rule sets f = W - 1 - i with i the narrowest signed integer width containing the kernel absmax. All eight fp32-s3 attention kernels have absmax 0.362-0.411 < 0.46875, so i = -1 and therefore f = W. Only W = 5 reproduces f = 5; W = 6 would give f = 6, one bit finer than the target.",
  "why_activations_stay_at_8": "Both comparators (W8A8 and the A2 W=8 control) feed the attention einsums with 8-bit operands (*_iq_t). Running the ladder at width 5 would coarsen activations to 5 bits and change the multiplier operand width, reintroducing the very confound this arm exists to remove. convert_fp32.py therefore gained an additive --weight-width flag (default None == historical behaviour) so the weight lattice moves alone.",
